## Lore

The Nightbane are the central characters of the Dark Day invasion: ordinary
people - mostly teenagers and young adults - who discovered on the day of their
Becoming that their human bodies hid something far stranger and more powerful.
From that day they have been at war with the supernatural, whether they wanted
it or not.

Every Nightbane wears two shapes. The human Facade is the body they grew up in;
the Morphus is a monstrous, alien form unique to each of them. Nobody is sure
which is the "real" one, and most Nightbane have to settle that question for
themselves - humans gifted with a shadow shape, or aliens masquerading as
humans. Some who chose the second answer have turned their backs on humanity;
those who chose the first use their powers to heal and protect.

No two Morphus look alike. Many believe the form reflects the Nightbane''s
personality, or even embodies its soul, beautiful and ugly alike.

A Nightbane takes one of four skill packages - Basic for an untrained student,
or the Resistance, Nocturne/Seeker/Lightbringer or Warlord training of a Faction
- or learns magic as a Nightbane Sorcerer or Nightbane Mystic.

## GM Notes

**Creating the character.** Most Nightbane were normal young people until the
Becoming, and their human personality and outlook do not vanish with it; the
contrast between a monstrous appearance and a human heart is a main theme of the
game. Before rolling dice, ask where the character grew up, what schooling he
had, where he was on Dark Day, what the first Becoming was like, how he met
others of his kind, how friends and family reacted, and whether he belongs to a
Faction and why. Two to four years after Dark Day the Factions are well defined;
at the start of the invasion only two or three exist.

**Two sets of numbers.** Combat bonuses are kept separately for the Facade and
the Morphus. The Facade fights with whatever hand to hand skill the character
learned; the Morphus fights at martial arts by instinct, with one more attack
and Supernatural Strength damage.

**Skill packages are guidelines.** A G.M. may allow skills outside a package for
a convincing background reason, and is under no obligation to.

**Alliances and allies.** Depending on affiliation, Nightbane may work with
humans, Guardians, vampires, Wampyrs and others, but most of a character''s
allies are other Nightbane.

**Average life span.** Unknown. Many are known to have lived over a thousand
years, and some are rumored to be over 5,000 years old.
